BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trans Picnic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260726T160000
DESCRIPTION: Omaha TLC presents Trans PicnicTrans Picnic is scheduled for July 26th at Elmwood Park. Be sure to request off of work if you need in order to join us 😁If you have any questions, suggestions, or concerns, feel free to dm us! And if you'd like to help with this or future events, let us know!!🌻Details🌻When: July 26th from 3-8pm (show up early if you'd like to help us set up!)Where: Elmwood Park, navigate to Elmwood Park Parking, you'll see us!Food: Potluck style! We will have burgers, hotdogs, and vegetarian options. Bring your own food to share as well if you're able! (Vegan and/or gluten free options are encouraged, but not required) We will have cards to write out ingredients for your dish.Activities: We will have some yard games, crafting activies, and other fun games to play. We'll have scheduled events for anyone who wants to participate. Feel free to bring your own games/activities to share too.Extras: Masks are encouraged and provided! There is a sidewalk ramp leading to the picnic table pad and plenty of seating at the tables. There are portable bathrooms closeby, but I believe the pavillion bathrooms are locked 😕 let us know if that could pose any issues and we will work on a solution! Pets are welcome on a leash. Bring picnic blankets and/or lawn chairs if you're able (the picnic tables at the park will have activities on them and some will be reserved for any disabled individuals who request it) \n ID: [ 49971793-9efa-4997-93fc-544d206eae10 ] \n LINK: [ https://actionnetwork.org/events/trans-picnic ].
STATUS: Published = true
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Community Hike at Hitchcock Nature Center
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260722T153000
DESCRIPTION: Join us at Hitchcock Nature Center this Wednesday July 22nd at 3:30 PM for a 4-mile hike through the Loess Hills of Iowa! Max elevation will be about 700ft so if you are sensitive to that please keep it in mind. The cost for this is $5 per vehicle for admission, so carpooling with some friends is definitely encouraged! Come and enjoy nature and time with other members of the community.Directions: From Interstate I-29 take the Crescent exit and travel east to The Old Lincoln Highway. Hitchcock Nature Center is located 5 miles north of Crescent off of Old Lincoln Highway. \n ID: [ 9e4c3c2d-d65f-49f0-80c8-24241f4932dc ] \n LINK: [ https://actionnetwork.org/events/community-hike-at-hitchcock-nature-center ].
STATUS: Published = true
END:VEVENT
